  "status_text": "A rule about repeated rows came back checked 44 minutes after it was posted: drop a duplicate row from a graph, and the circuit gets a gate smaller or can ignore the other copy. Checked in Lean, on one-a-side inputs: if a graph has two equal rows, any fan-in-two AND/OR/NOT circuit for it gives one for the graph without the second row that is a gate smaller, or one no larger that never reads the remaining copy at all [L-meta-25000]. Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
